From bde857fdf1e6095d65c035bb463312f67b46eda3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KSMubasshir <ksmubasshir@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:24:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add E2SM-MOB service model reporting handover KPIs over E2

The RIC agent's models expose no handover information: KPM carries
per-UE radio and traffic metrics only, and nothing reports measurement
reports or S1/intra-eNB handover outcomes.

RRC now keeps cumulative handover counters (S1 source/target attempt,
preparation success/failure, execution success/failure; intra-eNB;
re-establishment; measurement reports), each UE's handover state and
last MeasurementReport, and a log of the latest 64 handover and
re-establishment events, exported through rrc_metrics_t.  The source
side counts success when the MME releases the context with cause
successful-handover, which S1AP now passes to RRC.

The new ORAN-E2SM-MOB model (OID 1.3.6.1.4.1.53148.1.1.2.102, RAN
function 4, after the existing ones) sends these as periodic
indications; each subscription gets the events since its previous
report.  Its ASN.1 is in-tree and generated at build time like
NexRAN's.  Build option ENABLE_RIC_AGENT_MOB (default ON).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
